WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:01.968
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.667
We are hanging out
with Fred Armisen.

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:05.567
"Los Espookys" tomorrow night.

00:00:05.567 --> 00:00:07.868
HBO, HBO Max.

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:10.200
You're not only just
a talented comedian,

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.000
you're also
a very talented musician.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.300
And every time you're here,
we ask you to do

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.334
a new musical impression for us.

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:19.167
So, this time you brought us
some drum impressions.

00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:20.801
-Yes.
-I've never seen these before,

00:00:20.801 --> 00:00:24.200
but we have a drum kit ready for
you whenever you're ready.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.100
-Great.
-Go for it.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.334
Thank you, Fred Armisen.

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:28.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:34.434
-Alright, so, the first
impression I'm going to do

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:37.601
is an Instagram drummer.

00:00:37.601 --> 00:00:41.434
Like, for some reason
on my feed, I get these videos

00:00:41.434 --> 00:00:44.300
of drummers who like to do
close-ups of their kit.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.300
And there's a lot of, like,

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.634
gimmicks and stuff
on their drums.

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:51.701
So, every time -- so,
Instagram's a little bit like...

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:01.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:03.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:04.534
-Nice.

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:11.534
-When I was a teenager, I think
like a lot of -- I'm just going

00:01:11.534 --> 00:01:13.834
to do, like, drumming
through different ages.

00:01:13.834 --> 00:01:18.434
And I think teenagers tend to,
like, lean in on fills instead

00:01:18.434 --> 00:01:20.067
of the beat,
like the regular beat.

00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:23.334
So I used to play kind of like
barely doing a beat, like...

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:35.200
That was, like,
teenage drumming.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.434
Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:37.434 --> 00:01:39.334
You know, like, really
struggling with it.

00:01:39.334 --> 00:01:41.834
Then in my 20s,
I was in this band,

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:44.667
and we played really frenetic,
fast music.

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:46.934
And I just feel like I was just
out to prove that I could play

00:01:46.934 --> 00:01:48.467
quickly with a lot of changes,
like...

00:01:54.634 --> 00:01:57.467
That kind of thing.
Like just really, really busy.

00:01:57.467 --> 00:02:00.434
That's, like, you know,
in my 20s.

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:04.234
And then in my 30s, less toms,
less fills,

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:06.200
but, like, lots of cymbals
to make up for it, so like...

00:02:13.667 --> 00:02:17.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
Then -- Thanks.

00:02:17.501 --> 00:02:21.100
Then in my 40s, no cymbals,
high hat very closed,

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:23.133
and, like, really leaning in
on the kick drum, so like...

00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:27.734
This is like 40s.

00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:33.534
That's like 40s drumming.

00:02:33.534 --> 00:02:35.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah, thanks.

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:40.300
And so now in my 50s --
and this is the truth.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:42.334
This is, like, the groove
I most like to play.

00:02:42.334 --> 00:02:44.434
This is the volume I like.

00:02:44.434 --> 00:02:46.200
I'm most comfortable doing this.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:54.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.701 --> 00:02:56.033
And --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:58.334
Thanks. It's really --

00:02:58.334 --> 00:03:00.467
I love that -- I love that feel.

00:03:00.467 --> 00:03:03.534
So, I think with that
trajectory, as I, you know, go

00:03:03.534 --> 00:03:05.701
into my 60s and 70s,
I think my drumming style

00:03:05.701 --> 00:03:07.234
is going to be this.

00:03:08.701 --> 00:03:17.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:17.234 --> 00:03:19.300
-Fred Armisen, everybody.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.901
Season two of "Los Espookys"

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:25.634
premieres tomorrow
on HBO and HBO Max.

00:03:25.634 --> 00:03:27.634
We'll be right back
with Letitia Wright.

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:29.067
Stick around, everybody.

00:03:29.067 --> 00:03:35.100
♪♪

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:41.133
♪♪

